type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki
list: obsolete archived

Allowed values for the `lifecycle` field, in display order.

`lifecycle` says whether a tiddler is still alive. An empty field means //active//, so it is only ever filled on the few tiddlers that have left circulation: list the live ones with `[!has[lifecycle]]`.

It is independent of `maturity`: a stable tiddler can become obsolete or be archived, and keeps its maturity when it does.

To customise the vocabulary, edit the `list` field above (source file: `src/base-fields/vocab/lifecycle.tid`), then add the matching entries to `vocab/icons.multids` and to `language/<lang>/vocab.multids`. A value with no translation falls back to its own slug; a value with no icon simply renders without one.
